+# Task: erase, persistence and storage estimates (P02-14) · Phase: 02 · Owner: builder (wt-p02s5)
+
+<!-- Save as platewise/docs/notes/P<nn>/<slug>.md. Write everything above "Compare checklist"
+BEFORE writing code, in your own words. Never paste or paraphrase the reference line by line. -->
+
+Read (reference @ `10e14b67`): `A/ui/settings/SettingsViewModel.kt` lines 1469–1500 (the order of
+"delete all data"); research spec `06-settings-data.md` §3.15, §3.18, §5 (Delete All Data on the
+web, storage card, persistence) and §6 R06.5, R06.10, R06.19; decision D-16.8; the landed bus
+(`src/data/bus.ts`, message `erase`) and `openDb` (closes on `versionchange`). The web parts have
+no reference counterpart. No Evidence ids.
+
+What it does (own words): "Erase everything" removes every trace of the person's data from this
+browser. It first tells the app's other open tabs (an `erase` message on the bus) so they close
+their database connection and show a notice, closes this tab's connection, deletes the whole
+`platewise` database (every table: diary, photos, keys, settings, quarantine, meta), then removes
+the app's own Cache Storage entries and `localStorage` keys, both named with the `platewise-`
+prefix; anything else on the origin is left alone. A tab that does not let go makes the delete
+`blocked`: we broadcast `erase` once more and give the other tabs a moment; if the delete still
+waits, the caller is told (so the screen can ask the person to close other tabs), and the queued
+delete finishes on its own once they close. Storage helpers (D-16.8, R06.19): after the first
+logged entry the app asks the browser to keep its storage (`navigator.storage.persist()`), once
+per device, and records that it asked; Settings shows whether storage is persistent and how much
+is used of the quota. Browsers without these APIs read as `unknown`, never an error.
+
+Inputs → outputs:
+- `src/data/wipe.ts`: `eraseEverything({ db?, name?, indexedDB?, bus?, caches?, localStorage?,
+  pause? })` → `{ kind: 'erased' }` | `{ kind: 'blocked', finished }` (finished resolves to
+  `'erased'` or `'failed'` once the queued delete ends) | `{ kind: 'failed', error }`.
+  `closeOnErase(db, { bus?, onErase? })` → a stop function: in every tab, an `erase` posted by
+  another tab closes this tab's connection and calls `onErase` (the notice). `OWNED_PREFIX`.
+- `src/data/storage.ts`: `requestPersistence(db, { storage? })` → `'persistent' | 'best-effort' |
+  'unknown'`; `persistenceStatus({ storage? })` → the same three states; `estimate({ storage? })`
+  → `{ usage, quota }` or null.
+
+Files: created `src/data/wipe.ts`, `src/data/wipe.test.ts`, `src/data/storage.ts`,
+`src/data/storage.test.ts`, this note.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- Another tab of this build: its `openDb` closes on `versionchange` and `closeOnErase` closes it on
+  the bus message, so the delete is not blocked.
+- A tab that keeps its connection (an older build, a frozen tab) → `blocked` → broadcast again,
+  wait once (`pause`, about 1.5 s by default; tests pass their own) → still waiting → reported as
+  `blocked` with `finished`; the delete request stays queued and completes when that tab closes.
+  An IndexedDB delete cannot be cancelled and a second delete request would only queue behind the
+  first, so "retry" means broadcast again and wait one more round on the same request.
+- The delete fails (`error` event) or IndexedDB is missing → `failed`; caches and `localStorage`
+  are then left as they are, so a second try repeats the whole erase.
+- No Cache Storage (`caches` missing: insecure page, test environment) or no `localStorage`
+  (blocked by the browser; even reading `window.localStorage` can throw) → those steps are
+  skipped; a failing cache delete is ignored (caches hold only app files, rebuilt on demand).
+- Only names starting with `platewise-` go: other apps on the same origin keep their caches and
+  keys.
+- Our own tab posts `erase` too: `closeOnErase` ignores messages from this tab (the erasing tab
+  moves to onboarding itself).
+- `requestPersistence` asked twice (in sequence or at the same time, also from two tabs) → one
+  `persist()` call: concurrent calls in a tab share one ask, and the "asked" setting is claimed in
+  a transaction before asking, so a second tab does not ask again. Already persistent → no ask.
+- `persist()` or `persisted()` missing or throwing → `unknown`; `estimate()` missing, throwing or
+  answering without numbers → null. Nothing here throws.
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- The order follows the web plan (bus, close, delete database, caches, local storage) instead of
+  the reference's (forget backup session, clear the store, clear keys, delete photos): one database
+  delete removes the store, keys and photos together. Forgetting a running backup (R06.5) and
+  cancelling reminder timers (R06.10) are services that do not exist yet; the Erase action in
+  P09-15 does them before calling `eraseEverything`.
+- "Records the answer": the device-only setting `storage.persistAsked` becomes true when we ask
+  (so we never ask twice on this device); the answer itself is not copied into the database,
+  because `navigator.storage.persisted()` reports it at any time and a stored copy could go stale
+  (the person can revoke it in the browser).
+- The `erase` broadcast is the notice channel; closing also happens through `openDb`'s own
+  `versionchange` handler, so a tab that missed the message still lets go.
+- Dependencies (`indexedDB`, `caches`, `localStorage`, `navigator.storage`, the bus, the pause) are
+  options with the browser's objects as defaults, so tests use fakes and no timers.
+
+Tests we will write:
+- erase deletes every table (reopen → all empty) and our cache entries and `localStorage` keys but
+  not foreign ones.
+- A second open connection receives `erase` and closes; its notice runs once; a message from its
+  own tab is ignored.
+- A tab that keeps its connection → `blocked` after one retry (erase posted twice, one pause);
+  closing that tab finishes the delete.
+- A tab that lets go on the second broadcast → `erased`.
+- A failing delete → `failed`, caches and keys kept.
+- `persist()` called once when asked twice in a row and twice at once; the setting records the
+  ask; already persistent → no ask; denied → `best-effort`.
+- Missing `navigator.storage` → status `unknown` and `requestPersistence` `unknown` without
+  throwing (R06.19); throwing APIs → `unknown`; `estimate` with and without the API.
+
+Compare checklist (filled after the rewrite; reopened `A/ui/settings/SettingsViewModel.kt` lines
+1469–1500):
+- [ ] Everything the reference's delete-all clears is gone after erase (tested in `<file>`)
+- Deliberate differences: <…>
+- Not taken: <…>
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+
+## Status
